# Internationalization

The app ships four locales: `en`, `de`, `hr`, `sr` (`LOCALES` in `@shared/types`).
English is the source of truth — `MessageKey` is `keyof typeof en`, and
`Messages` forces every other catalog to define exactly the same keys.

## Adding or changing a message

- Add the key to `en.ts` first, then to `de.ts`, `hr.ts`, and `sr.ts`. A missing
  or misspelled key is a compile error in that catalog — don't leave it untranslated
  or duplicated from English.
- Use `{name}` placeholders for interpolation; `translate` substitutes them from
  `TranslationParams`. Keep placeholder names identical across locales.
- Register a new locale by extending `LOCALES`, adding its catalog to `messages`,
  and adding an autonym entry to `LOCALE_OPTIONS`.

Consume translations in components via `useTranslation()`, never by importing
catalogs directly.
